quran[13]{c,v,t}:
  21,45,Say: ‘I only warn you through revelation.’ But the deaf will not hear the call whenever they are warned.
  21,46,"Yet if a (minor) breath of your Lord’s punishment touches them, they will surely say: ‘Woe to us! Truly, we have been wrongdoers.’"
  21,47,"And We shall set up the scales of justice on the Day of Resurrection. And no soul shall be wronged in the least. Even if it be the weight of a grain of mustard seed, We shall produce it, and We suffice as Reckoners."
  21,48,"And indeed, We gave Musa (Moses) and Harun (Aaron) the standard (to distinguish between right and wrong), a light and a reminder for those who are God-conscious."
  21,49,"Those who fear their Lord without seeing, and they are apprehensive of the Hour."
  21,50,This (Qur’an) is a blessed Reminder that We have revealed. Are you (all) going to deny it?
  21,51,"We had indeed bestowed upon Ibrahim (Abraham) rectitude of his conduct long before, and We knew him."
  21,52,When he said to his (foster) father and his people: ‘What are these idols to which you are so devoted (in worship)?’
  21,53,They said: ‘We found our fathers worshipping them.’
  21,54,"He said: ‘Surely, you and your fathers have been in clear error.’"
  21,55,"They said: ‘Have you brought us the truth, or are you just joking?’"
  21,56,"He said: ‘Instead, your Lord is the Lord of the heavens and the earth, Who brought them into existence. And I am among those who bear witness to that."
  21,57,"By Allah, I shall surely plan against your idols after you have gone away, turning your backs.’"
